  A: [{
    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Night the Mountain Shook', s: 'Kichik qishloq zilziladan keyin qanday birlashdi',
    p: [
      ['It was a quiet evening in the mountains. The sky was [overcast], and a light [drizzle] fell. In the morning there had been a [scorching] heat, and the weather changed [unpredictably|unpredictably]. A [gust] of wind opened the window of the school. Soon a [downpour] began, followed by a [thunderstorm]. Hail fell, [hail] and then [sleet] covered the road. People said it was only a [gale] and that every [frost] would pass. That year people had heard about a [blizzard] in the north, a [hurricane] on the coast and a [tornado] in the south.',
       'Tog‘lardagi tinch kechqurun edi. Osmon bulutli edi va mayda yomg‘ir yog‘ayotgandi. Ertalab jazirama issiq bo‘lgan, ob-havo esa kutilmagan tarzda o‘zgardi. Shamol turtkisi maktab derazasini ochib yubordi. Tez orada jala boshlandi, keyin momaqaldiroqli bo‘ron keldi. Do‘l yog‘di, keyin qorli yomg‘ir yo‘lni qopladi. Odamlar bu shunchaki kuchli shamol, har bir qirov o‘tib ketadi, deyishdi. O‘sha yili shimolda qor bo‘roni, qirg‘oqda dovul va janubda tornado haqida eshitishgan edi.'],
      ['At midnight the ground began to shake. An [earthquake] of high [magnitude] struck the village, and several [aftershocks|aftershock] followed. A [landslide] blocked the road, and an [avalanche] fell on the northern slope. It was a [devastating] and [destructive] event, a real [a bolt from the blue]. “[Batten down the hatches|Batten down the hatches]!” someone shouted. The old school became a [shelter]. It was clear that people, especially children, were [vulnerable].',
       'Yarim kechada yer silkina boshladi. Katta kuchli zilzila qishloqqa urildi va bir nechta takroriy silkinish bo‘ldi. Ko‘chki yo‘lni to‘sdi, shimoliy qiyalikka qor ko‘chkisi tushdi. Bu vayron qiluvchi va halokatli voqea edi, haqiqiy kutilmagan musibat. «Qiyinchilikka tayyorlaning!» deb qichqirdi kimdir. Eski maktab boshpanaga aylandi. Odamlar, ayniqsa bolalar himoyasiz ekani ayon edi.'],
      ['Rescuers had to [evacuate] the whole village. The roads were [hazardous] after the [torrential] rain, and [debris] and [rubble] lay everywhere. The [survivors|survivor] helped each other, and [casualties|casualty] were few, thanks to the early warning. In the morning the first [relief] trucks arrived, followed by [aid] from other regions. A [tsunami] warning on the radio from the coast turned out to be false. The only [eruption] was the joy of the people who were saved.',
       'Qutqaruvchilar butun qishloqni evakuatsiya qilishga majbur bo‘ldi. Jaladan keyin yo‘llar xavfli edi, hamma yerda vayronalar va tosh-chiqindi yotardi. Omon qolganlar bir-biriga yordam berdi, erta ogohlantirish tufayli jabrlanuvchilar kam edi. Ertalab birinchi yordam yuk mashinalari yetib keldi, keyin boshqa hududlardan ko‘mak keldi. Qirg‘oqdan radioda sunami haqida ogohlantirish yolg‘on bo‘lib chiqdi. Yagona otilish saqlanib qolgan odamlarning quvonchi edi.'],
      ['Months later the villagers began to [rebuild] their homes, school by school. “[Every cloud has a silver lining|Every cloud has a silver lining],” the old teacher said. “We have learned to be prepared.” A year later a hurricane warning came, but the town was ready, [come rain or shine|come rain or shine]. Children laughed again and felt [on cloud nine|on cloud nine] at the new school opening. The mountain was still there, but the people were stronger.',
       'Oylar o‘tgach qishloq aholisi uylarni qayta qura boshladi, maktab ortidan maktab. «Har yomonlikda yaxshilik bor, — dedi keksa o‘qituvchi. — Biz tayyor bo‘lishni o‘rgandik.» Bir yildan keyin dovul haqida ogohlantirish keldi, lekin shahar har qanday ob-havoda tayyor edi. Yangi maktab ochilishida bolalar yana kulishdi va baxtdan osmonda edi. Tog‘ hali ham o‘sha yerda edi, lekin odamlar kuchliroq edi.']
    ],
    q: [
      ['What happened at midnight?', ['An earthquake struck the village.', 'A fire started.', 'The river flooded.'], 0],
      ['What became a shelter?', ['The old school', 'A cave', 'A church'], 0],
      ['Why were casualties few?', ['Because of an early warning', 'Because of luck only', 'Because nobody lived there'], 0],
      ['What arrived in the morning?', ['Relief trucks', 'Tourists', 'Journalists only'], 0],
      ['What did the old teacher say?', ['Every cloud has a silver lining.', 'It was a mistake.', 'Leave the village.'], 0]
    ]
  }],
